.SH NAME
anpu-import - Import Burp, ZAP, or HAR results as findings


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu import  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Normalize a third-party artifact into ANPU findings.

.PP
Formats (auto-detected from extension when --format is omitted):
  .xml  Burp Suite export
  .json ZAP JSON report (zap-baseline -J)
  .har  HTTP Archive capture (endpoints + 5xx notes)

.PP
Examples:
  anpu import burp.xml --json
  anpu import zap.json --output imported.json
  anpu import session.har --target https://example.com/


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--format\fP=""
	burp, zap, or har (default: from file extension)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for import

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print findings as JSON

.PP
\fB--output\fP=""
	write normalized findings+endpoints JSON here

.PP
\fB--target\fP=""
	target label for imported findings


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


